    "description": "Latency is the delay between a request being made and the response being received. It is typically measured in milliseconds and is a key indicator of perceived application responsiveness.\n\nSources of latency include network round-trip time, database query time, I/O wait, and processing overhead. Reducing latency involves techniques such as caching, connection pooling, query optimization, and co-locating services.",
